	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/video_settings/first_person/weapon_body/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Draws your weapon, your hands and what they hold. Hide clears the view; you still fire, reload and hear them."/>
		<string text="How wide your weapon and hands are drawn, in degrees across a 16:9 screen: wider draws them smaller. Default keeps the weapon's own view.|Click the number (or press A) to type any from 20 to 150."/>
		<string text="Moves and turns your weapon and hands on the screen, for every weapon and, in a game, for the one you hold."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Your legs when you look down, moving as you run: your body as the others see it."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="When your shield takes a hit, its flare shows on your first-person arms too, as on your body, and fades as it does there. A full, untouched shield shows nothing.|An overshield stays lit on them with Overshield on, below."/>
		<string text="Your shield's flare in an armor color, whatever your armor. Only you see it. Default keeps its own."/>
		<string text="An overshield stays lit for as long as it lasts, in its own color, on your body and, with Arm Shields, your arms. Off draws it as the original did. Online: the host's choice.|Off in Pro 2v2 games, for everyone."/>
		<string text="The overshield's color as its layers drain, as your shield meter shows them: green while the green layer lasts, then red. Red keeps it red throughout."/>
	</strings>
